GROUP              TOPIC              PARTITION  CURRENT-OFFSET  LOG-END-OFFSET  LAG             CONSUMER-ID                                              HOST            CLIENT-ID
payment-service-v2 outbox.event.Order 0          6               6               0               kafka-python-3.0.11-6d411717-b480-4057-8a4b-e9382f973c2a /172.22.0.13    kafka-python-3.0.11
=== real finding ===
3 payment-service replicas running, but only 1 consumer group member is actually assigned
(topic 'outbox.event.Order' has exactly 1 partition - real Kafka constraint: a consumer group
can have at most as many ACTIVE consumers as partitions; the other 2 replicas sit fully idle,
confirmed via the single CONSUMER-ID row above with LAG=0). This is the real reason production
Kafka topics are provisioned with multiple partitions BEFORE scaling consumers - scaling
consumer replicas alone does nothing without enough partitions to spread across.
